STEP 2 — CONCEPT
  product:   Verso
  one-liner: a collaborative interface design tool that loads every file mirrored, so your drawing
             hand never sits on top of the work.
  angle:     handedness treated as an unsolved layout problem. The fix (flip everything, forever,
             including exports) is confidently wrong. Right-handed collaborators are a supported
             read-only population. Paper is framed as a competitor with better palm dynamics.
  anti-ai-slop invoked before writing any copy. Zero em dashes across concept, landing, and demo.
             No throat-clearing, no corrective antithesis, no gift-wrapped closer.

STEP 3 — PLAN (visual direction)
  ui-ux-pro-max invoked. Its --design-system query returned an Event/Conference pattern with a
  black + pink "vibrant block-based" system, which did not fit a design-tool product page, so the
  returned pattern was discarded and only its rule categories were carried forward (contrast,
  focus states, tabular figures, 44px targets, 150-300ms transitions, reduced-motion, no emoji
  icons). Style, palette, and fonts were selected directly.

  style:     Mirrored Swiss modernist design-tool site, paper daylight mode. Right-anchored grid,
             0px radii, hairline rules, solid ultramarine floods, no shadows and no gradients.
             Section numerals count down (04 03 02 01) and render mirrored via scaleX(-1);
             pricing runs most expensive first.
  palette:   Paper / Ultramarine / Rationed Fuchsia
             primary #1F2ED6, accent #D6006B, bg #F1F1EE, fg #16161A, muted #78786F, ink #0B0B0D
  fonts:     display Archivo, body Figtree, telemetry DM Mono
  archetype: collaborative design-tool product page, mirrored
  signature: the header "Flip back" control, which mirrors the entire page for 1.8 seconds, raises
             a fuchsia re-assessment notice, and reverts itself.

  ANTI-SAMENESS CHECK vs the last 7 entries — no collision on style, palette, or font pair:
    2026-08-08 replit-for-red-pandas          claymorphic light   / rust+moss     / Bricolage + Red Hat Text
    2026-08-07 midjourney-for-hedgehogs       aurora glass dark   / lilac+moss    / Fraunces + Outfit
    2026-08-06 hinge-for-divorced-dads        heritage catalog    / forest+rust   / Besley + Work Sans
    2026-08-05 bumble-for-penguins            sticker poster      / yolk+ice blue / Nunito + DM Sans
    2026-08-04 tinder-for-seagulls            nautical chart      / red+teal      / Libre Franklin + Public Sans
    2026-08-03 steam-for-yogis                storefront dark     / blue+matcha   / Marcellus + Inter
    2026-08-02 neuralink-for-amateur-somm.    didone label dark   / gold+mint     / Bodoni Moda + Jost
  Swiss modernist is unused in the window; magenta/fuchsia is the first non-green, non-rust accent
  in seven entries; Archivo, Figtree, and DM Mono are all unused in the window.

STEP 4 — IMAGES
  budget: 4 available, 3 spent, 1 deliberately left unspent.
  allocation rationale:
    hero      — SKIPPED. The direction is purely typographic; a photograph would soften the grid
                poster and fight the ultramarine floods.
    demo      — SKIPPED. demo_screen_concept is a design-editor console (tool rail, layers list,
                inspector), not photo-shaped. Console demos get no assets per the image guidelines.
    headshots — 3 generated, the always-applicable fallback slot.

  headshot-1.webp  attempt 1/2  JUDGE: PASS. Correct subject, deadpan, paper-white seamless
                   backdrop reading close to #F1F1EE, small ultramarine garment accent, no text
                   artifacts, no generic-render tells. 8,406 bytes.
  headshot-2.webp  attempt 1/2  JUDGE: PASS. Same criteria. 7,734 bytes.
  headshot-3.webp  attempt 1/2  JUDGE: PASS. Same criteria. 8,844 bytes.
  All three cropped to 320x320 WebP with --delete-input; raw PNGs removed. No regenerations,
  no drops. 3 of the day's 10-call cap consumed.

  NEAR-MISS: all three subjects hold the pencil in their right hand as rendered, despite the
  prompt asking for the left. Rather than burn regenerations, both pages render the headshots
  with transform: scaleX(-1). That corrects the handedness and is on-concept for a site whose
  entire premise is mirroring. No image was regenerated or dropped on this basis.

STEP 5 — BUILD LANDING
  frontend-design invoked before writing markup. Landing page is self-contained: inline CSS,
  inline JS, Google Fonts via <link>, no frameworks, no build step, no hotlinked assets.
  Sections: inverted masthead (nav left, wordmark hard right), right-anchored hero with the
  mirror axis and a bleeding mirrored numeral, hairline telemetry strip, CSS-built mirrored
  editor plate, three feature columns numbered 03/02/01, three testimonial plates carrying the
  headshots, a pricing ladder running Ambidextrous / Sinistral / Southpaw, closing CTA band on
  ink, footer with the back link to /.
  Accessibility: fuchsia focus-visible rings, 44px+ hit areas, alt text on every headshot,
  prefers-reduced-motion disables the axis draw, reveals, and the page flip.

  frontend-design flags "broadsheet with hairline rules and zero radius" as one of three current
  AI-design defaults, which is adjacent to this direction. Kept it because the brief pinned the
  direction, and the mirroring conceit, ultramarine floods, rationed fuchsia telemetry, and the
  self-reverting flip control are what carry the page rather than the hairlines.

STEP 6 — BUILD DEMO
  demo.html is the mirrored Verso editor. Toolbar, layers, and inspector pinned right; the
  artboard sits left and renders scaleX(-1). Working interactivity, all client-side:
    - cursor and touch movement across the artboard lays permanent stepped graphite smudge nodes,
      driving live stroke and coverage counters (node pool capped at 420 for scroll performance)
    - per-layer visibility toggles, except Smudge Layer whose control is disabled and answers
      with "The Smudge Layer stays on. It is the product."
    - five tools (Move, Frame, Pen, Palm, Text) each swapping the inspector fields and its note
    - the X field rejects positive values and inverts them, since X counts leftward
    - "Flip back" opens a modal with one selectable option, Escape and scrim close, focus is
      restored to the trigger, and confirming reports "Assessment matches file. No change applied."
    - collaborator avatars reuse the three headshots with verified / pending / read-only states
  Top-left chrome carries the "back to the pitch" link to ./index.html.

